  "notes": "USAGE:\nOften used with に{対|たい}して to mark what is being argued against. The noun form {反論|はんろん} is also very common (e.g., {反論|はんろん}がある 'there is an objection').\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- 〜に{対|たい}して{反論|はんろん}する (argue back against ~)\n- {反論|はんろん}の{余地|よち}がない (no room for rebuttal)\n- {反論|はんろん}を{述|の}べる (state a counterargument)\n- {激|はげ}しく{反論|はんろん}する (argue back fiercely)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {反対|はんたい}する: to oppose — broader; can mean opposing a plan or idea without necessarily presenting a reasoned argument\n- {否定|ひてい}する: to deny — focuses on rejecting a claim as false\n- {言|い}い{返|かえ}す: to talk back — more colloquial and can imply rudeness",
